 "_why": [
  "THE portal rule (MS19, migration 590; two-sided since 597; status since 657), one table read by",
  "both languages. The status switch (any / active / inactive) is the PROPERTY's own is_active, the",
  "status every surface draws. A portal set P asks for an ad on P in that same status: active = an",
  "active ad on P (active_sources), otherwise any ad on P (all_sources: an ended property has only",
  "ended ads); several portals = any of them. AND it has no ad on any EXCLUDED portal: any ad, live",
  "or ended (all_sources), or only live ones when excluded_active_only (active_sources); independent",
  "of the status switch and of a broker. tests/test_portal_rule.py runs `cases` through",
  "public.portal_status_matches, both aggregate RPCs and both property grains' compiled portal",
  "rule (the Watchdog's and the agents' search); queries.test.ts runs them through",
  "applyPortalRule. `broker_cases` put the",
  "portal side on ONE broker's ads (portal and broker together = one ad) while the status stays the",
  "property's: the DB lane seeds the ads, runs the broker lookup and the property's status. An",
  "exclusion stays on the property under a broker, so it has no broker case."
 ],
